cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this formalization, please cite it as below, and cite the paper
  it formalizes for the mathematics.
type: software
title: >-
  BKT asymptotics for the quenched free energy of hierarchical pinning:
  Lean 4 formalization
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper "BKT asymptotics for the
  quenched free energy of hierarchical pinning" (Hexagon preprint
  2611.00654v1): all 24 numbered results, including the
  Berezinskii-Kosterlitz-Thouless asymptotics of the free energy near the
  critical point under a strict shift, with an explicit constant. The Lean
  code was produced by AI models (see README.md and FORMALIZATION_REPORT.md).
authors:
  - given-names: Igor
    family-names: Kortchemski
version: 0.1.0
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/igor-kortchemski/BKT-hierarchical-pinning"
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalization
  - disordered pinning
  - diamond hierarchical lattice
  - BKT transition
references:
  - type: generic
    status: preprint
    title: >-
      BKT asymptotics for the quenched free energy of hierarchical pinning
    authors:
      - name: ChatGPT
    year: 2026
    date-published: "2026-11-19"
    url: "https://hexagonmath.org/2611.00654v1"
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "hexagon:2611.00654v1"
    license: "CC-BY-4.0"
    notes: >-
      Hexagon preprint. The PDF credits “ChatGPT, directed by Igor
      Kortchemski”. Hexagon lists Igor Kortchemski as the contributor.
      The formalization was developed against the draft of 18 November 2026,
      then titled "BKT asymptotics for disordered pinning on the diamond
      hierarchical lattice".
